From 02c96bacbb13c83c555c27e6dee434c560e1e24f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 20:41:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0228: Replayable Quest Chains -- Replay Memories UI

Step (4) of the sequencing plan. First patch in this feature a player
can actually see and use.

DiscoveredQuestsPanel gains its first sub-tabs: Board (existing
content, untouched) and Replay Memories (new). 'chains' joins
TAB_SUBTABS in attention.ts as a 7th entry, with the same deep-link/
acknowledge-on-visit wiring every other sub-tabbed panel already has.

TierCard: all 6 saga bands + master unlock always visible regardless
of ownership. Owned bands list every covered chain as its own button,
disabled unless that chain is already in completedChains.

ChainReplayDetailModal: difficulty picker (ReplayDifficultyCircle,
same icon-with-fallback shape RaidsPanel's own DifficultyCircle uses)
plus a live loot-table view computed via scaleChainExclusiveItem
directly -- a pure function, so the preview always matches exactly
what a real drop would roll.

Caught and fixed a real mistake mid-build: a string replacement
accidentally clipped the existing ChainDetailModal's closing content
while inserting the new components. Caught by tsc --noEmit, not by
inspection; restored and reverified clean before proceeding.

Known scoping limit carried from step (3), not new here: 6 chains
have more than one guaranteed reward item; only the first is the
replay chase, matching QuestManager.resolve's own logic.

No changes to QuestManager, GuildManager, or persisted state -- purely
new UI consuming the engine actions/helpers patches 0224-0227 already
built.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and npx vite build both pass clean against
the properly re-based tree.
